# Registry and Loader Patterns

## Registry Pattern (OpenCart/CodeIgniter Style)

The Registry provides centralized service management with magic accessors.

### Accessing Services

#### In Controllers
```php
class MyController extends Controller
{
    public function index(): void
    {
        // Database access
        $users = $this->db->query("SELECT * FROM users")->fetchAll();
        
        // Session access
        $userId = $this->session->get('user_id');
        $this->session->set('key', 'value');
        
        // Cache access
        $data = $this->cache->get('cache_key');
        $this->cache->set('cache_key', $data, 3600);
        
        // Loader access
        $this->load->model('public/User/User');
        $this->load->library('security/Validator');
        $this->load->view('public/User/index', $data);
    }
}
```

#### In Models
```php
class UserModel extends Model
{
    public function getAllUsers(): array
    {
        // Database is available via $this->db
        $query = "SELECT * FROM users";
        return $this->db->query($query)->fetchAll();
    }
    
    public function getCachedUsers(): array
    {
        // Cache access
        if ($cached = $this->cache->get('all_users')) {
            return $cached;
        }
        
        $users = $this->getAllUsers();
        $this->cache->set('all_users', $users, 3600);
        return $users;
    }
}
```

### Available Services

| Service | Access | Description |
|---------|--------|-------------|
| Database | `$this->db` | Database connection and queries |
| Session | `$this->session` | Session management |
| Cache | `$this->cache` | Caching system |
| Loader | `$this->load` | Component loader |
| Router | `$this->router` | Router instance |
| Request | `$this->request` | HTTP request data |
| Response | `$this->response` | HTTP response |

### Registering Custom Services

#### In Bootstrap/Index
```php
$registry = Registry::getInstance();

// Register as singleton
$registry->singleton('mailer', function() {
    return new MailerService();
});

// Register with factory
$registry->register('logger', function() {
    return new Logger();
});

// Direct registration
$registry->set('config', $configObject);
```

#### Accessing Custom Services
```php
// In controller
$this->mailer->send($to, $subject, $message);
$this->logger->info('User logged in');
$config = $this->config->get('app.name');
```

## Loader Pattern (CodeIgniter Style)

The Loader provides convenient methods for loading framework components.

### Loading Models

#### Basic Model Loading
```php
// Load model
$this->load->model('public/Blog/Blog');

// Access model (auto-named with 'model_' prefix and lowercase)
$posts = $this->model_blog->getAllPosts();
```

#### Multiple Models
```php
$this->load->model('public/Blog/Blog');
$this->load->model('public/User/User');
$this->load->model('public/Comment/Comment');

$posts = $this->model_blog->getAllPosts();
$user = $this->model_user->getById(1);
$comments = $this->model_comment->getByPost($postId);
```

#### Model Naming Convention
```php
// Load 'public/Blog/Blog' → Access via $this->model_blog
// Load 'admin/User/User' → Access via $this->model_user
// Load 'api/Product/Product' → Access via $this->model_product
```

### Loading Views

#### Single View
```php
$this->load->view('public/Blog/index', $data);
```

#### Multiple Views (Common Pattern)
```php
$data = ['title' => 'Blog'];

$this->load->view('public/Common/header', $data);
$this->load->view('public/Blog/index', $data);
$this->load->view('public/Common/footer', $data);
```

#### View Path Format
```
"{role}/{module}/{viewname}"

Examples:
- "public/Home/home"      → Body/public/Home/Views/home.ct
- "admin/Dashboard/index" → Body/admin/Dashboard/Views/index.ct
- "public/Common/header"  → Body/public/Common/Views/header.ct
```

### Loading Libraries

#### Framework Libraries
```php
// Load library
$this->load->library('security/Validator');

// Use library
if ($this->validator->validate($data, $rules)) {
    // Valid
}
```

#### Custom Parameters
```php
// Load with constructor parameters
$this->load->library('Mailer', [
    'host' => 'smtp.example.com',
    'port' => 587
]);

$this->mailer->send($email);
```

#### Library Aliasing
```php
// Load with custom alias
$this->load->library('security/Validator', [], 'inputValidator');

// Access via alias
$this->inputValidator->validate($data);
```

### Loading Helpers

```php
// Load helper file
$this->load->helper('url');

// Helper functions now available globally
$url = base_url('path');
$link = anchor('path', 'Link Text');
```

## File Naming Conventions

### Controller Files
The framework supports multiple naming patterns:
- `about.php` (preferred - lowercase)
- `About.php`
- `AboutController.php`
- `aboutController.php`

Class name must be: `AboutController`

### Model Files
The framework supports:
- `AboutModel.php` (preferred - PascalCase)
- `About.php`
- `about.php`
- `about_model.php`

Class name must be: `AboutModel` or `About`

### View Files
Always lowercase with `.ct` extension:
- `index.ct`
- `about.ct`
- `show.ct`

## Dependency Injection

### Constructor Injection (Automatic)
```php
class BlogController extends Controller
{
    // Registry automatically injected by framework
    public function __construct($registry)
    {
        parent::__construct($registry);
        // Additional initialization
    }
}
```

### Service Resolution
```php
// The framework automatically:
// 1. Creates Registry instance
// 2. Registers core services
// 3. Injects Registry into controllers
// 4. Provides magic accessors

class MyController extends Controller
{
    public function index(): void
    {
        // All services available via magic accessors
        $this->db;      // Database
        $this->session; // Session
        $this->load;    // Loader
    }
}
```

## Best Practices

1. **Use magic accessors**: `$this->db` instead of `$this->registry->get('db')`
2. **Load models early**: Load at top of controller method
3. **Reuse models**: Load once, use multiple times in same request
4. **Name models consistently**: Follow role/module/model pattern
5. **Pass data to views**: Always prepare data array in controller
6. **Use Loader for components**: Don't require files manually
7. **Register services once**: In bootstrap/index, not per request
8. **Lazy load services**: Use factories for expensive operations
9. **Cache model data**: Use `$this->cache` for frequently accessed data
10. **Type hint services**: When extending classes, maintain type hints

## Common Patterns

### Controller with Multiple Models
```php
class DashboardController extends Controller
{
    public function index(): void
    {
        // Load multiple models
        $this->load->model('admin/User/User');
        $this->load->model('admin/Post/Post');
        $this->load->model('admin/Comment/Comment');
        
        // Get data from each
        $data = [
            'users' => $this->model_user->getRecentUsers(),
            'posts' => $this->model_post->getRecentPosts(),
            'comments' => $this->model_comment->getPendingComments()
        ];
        
        // Render view
        $this->load->view('admin/Dashboard/index', $data);
    }
}
```

### Model with Caching
```php
class PostModel extends Model
{
    public function getAllPosts(): array
    {
        $cacheKey = 'all_posts';
        
        // Try cache first
        if ($cached = $this->cache->get($cacheKey)) {
            return $cached;
        }
        
        // Get from database
        $posts = $this->db->query("SELECT * FROM posts")->fetchAll();
        
        // Cache for 1 hour
        $this->cache->set($cacheKey, $posts, 3600);
        
        return $posts;
    }
}
```

### Service with Session
```php
class AuthController extends Controller
{
    public function login(): void
    {
        // Validate credentials
        $this->load->model('public/User/User');
        $user = $this->model_user->authenticate($_POST['email'], $_POST['password']);
        
        if ($user) {
            // Set session
            $this->session->set('user_id', $user['id']);
            $this->session->set('role', $user['role']);
            
            // Redirect
            Router::redirectToRoute('dashboard');
        } else {
            $this->session->set('error', 'Invalid credentials');
            Router::redirectToRoute('login');
        }
    }
}
```
